Technical Log: Authentication Logic & Domain Qualification
The Challenge:
After successfully joining the Windows 11 Client to the phinehas.local domain, I attempted to log in as the Administrator. 
Despite resetting the password on the Domain Controller (DC01), the Client repeatedly rejected the credentials as "Incorrect Username or Password.

The Analysis:
I realized the Client was defaulting to its Local Security Authority (LSA). When typing just Administrator, 
the machine was attempting to authenticate against its local SAM database (CLI01\Administrator) 
rather than the Active Directory database on the Domain Controller.

The Resolution:
I used a Qualified Username by prepending the NetBIOS domain name: PHINEHAS\Administrator.

The Takeaway:
This confirmed that the "Trust Relationship" and DNS resolution between the Client and Domain Controller were functioning correctly. 
It highlighted the critical distinction between Local Accounts and Domain Accounts in a Windows environment.


